# Both ran in one shell invocation. The first confirms the Zig pin the script
# compares across commits and is not part of the script's own output; only the
# second line is. 80 first-parent commits give 79 steps, of which 51 leave every
# key input unchanged: the derived 64.6 percent the baseline uses as an assumed
# hit rate. HEAD was e76e235b.

# All three scripts were re-run during this preservation pass and reproduced
# their own output above exactly. Run each from the repository root, through
# standard input, so that node and git resolve the workspace's packages and
# history rather than a temporary directory's:
#
#   mise exec -- node --input-type=module-typescript \
#     < docs/evidence/u4/shard-signatures.ts.txt
#   mise exec -- node --input-type=module-typescript \
#     < docs/evidence/u4/upstream-signatures.ts.txt
#
# The churn script reads git history and hard-codes the U4 worktree path, so
# rewrite its cd target, and pin it to e76e235b because the branch's HEAD is one
# commit later:
#
#   sed -e 's#^cd /home/.*#cd "$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel)"#' \
#       -e 's/HEAD)$/e76e235b)/' docs/evidence/u4/key-churn.sh.txt \
#     | bash -s 80
